<title>UK: Czarnikow forecasts EU 1996/97 sugar output.</title>
<headline>Czarnikow forecasts EU 1996/97 sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union (EU) could exceed its 1995/96 beet sugar production this crop year and turn out 17.03 million tonnes raw value, Czarnikow Sugar said in its second estimate of the world balance on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a remarkable late season recovery in west European beet crops with until quite recently ideal weather alternating between mild sunny autumn days and showery spells,&quot; Czarnikow said.</p>
<p>It noted late crop improvements in Germany, Spain and Britain but said the French beet crop had not made good its earlier setbacks.</p>
<p>The EU produced 17.02 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>But despite the improved overall outlook for EU crops, a severe winter could still curtail the potential for the end of campaigns, it said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
